# Intervia Platform - AI Development Rules & Principles

## 🎯 CORE PHILOSOPHY: Mobile-First, Thumb-Friendly, Minimal Effort

### 1. MOBILE-FIRST DEVELOPMENT (CRITICAL)

#### Touch Target Requirements
- **MINIMUM touch target**: 44x44px (iOS/Android standard)
- **PREFERRED touch target**: 56-64px for primary actions
- **OPTIMAL touch target**: 120x120px for main feature cards
- All interactive elements MUST be easily reachable with thumb

#### Screen Size Strategy
- Design for mobile FIRST (320px - 768px)
- Tablet second (768px - 1024px)  
- Desktop last (1024px+)
- NEVER assume desktop first

#### Thumb Zone Optimization
```
EASY REACH (Priority 1):
- Bottom 1/3 of screen
- Center of screen
- Primary actions go here

STRETCH REACH (Priority 2):
- Middle 1/3 of screen
- Secondary actions

HARD REACH (Avoid):
- Top 1/3 of screen
- Top corners
- Only for occasional actions (logout, settings)
```

### 2. UI/UX PATTERNS

#### Navigation
- **Mobile (< 1024px)**: Fixed bottom navigation bar
  - 5 main items max
  - Large icons (24-28px)
  - Clear labels
  - Active state indicators
- **Desktop (≥ 1024px)**: Top navigation or sidebar
  - Bottom nav HIDDEN on desktop (`lg:hidden` class)

#### Content Sections

##### Hero Section
- **Mobile**: 
  - Large CTA button (h-14, full-width or centered)
  - Simplified search → Link to search page
  - Short heading (2-3 lines max)
  - Minimal text
- **Desktop**: 
  - Full search form allowed
  - Longer text acceptable

##### Quick Access Cards
- **Mobile**:
  - 3 columns max
  - Min height: 120px
  - Large icons (48-56px)
  - Distinct colors per category
  - Active feedback: `active:scale-95`
- **Desktop**:
  - Hover effects
  - Can expand to 4-5 columns

##### Content Lists (Products, Jobs, etc.)
- **Mobile**: 
  - Horizontal scroll with snap points
  - `overflow-x-auto` + `snap-x snap-mandatory`
  - Hide scrollbar but keep functionality
  - Card width: 120-160px
  - Show ALL items (no truncation)
- **Desktop**: 
  - Grid layout (3-5 columns)
  - Show limited items + "View All" link
  - Hover states

### 3. RESPONSIVE DESIGN RULES

#### Breakpoints (Tailwind)
```css
sm: 640px   /* Small tablets */
md: 768px   /* Tablets */
lg: 1024px  /* Desktop - PRIMARY BREAKPOINT */
xl: 1280px  /* Large desktop */
2xl: 1536px /* Extra large */
```

#### Mobile-Desktop Differences Template
```tsx
{/* Mobile: Simple/Scroll/Touch */}
<div className="lg:hidden">
  {/* Horizontal scroll, large tap targets, simplified */}
</div>

{/* Desktop: Complex/Grid/Hover */}
<div className="hidden lg:block">
  {/* Grid layout, hover effects, detailed */}
</div>
```

### 4. INTERACTION PATTERNS

#### Touch Feedback (Mobile)
```tsx
className="active:scale-95 transition-transform duration-150"
```

#### Hover Effects (Desktop Only)
```tsx
className="lg:hover:shadow-xl lg:hover:-translate-y-1"
```

#### Loading States
- Skeleton screens (no spinners)
- Optimistic UI updates
- Progressive loading

### 5. COLOR & VISUAL HIERARCHY

#### Primary Actions
- Emerald/Green: `emerald-500`, `emerald-600`
- High contrast
- Large size
- Bottom 1/3 of screen on mobile

#### Secondary Actions  
- Blue: `blue-500`
- Gray: `slate-600`
- Smaller size

#### Destructive Actions
- Red: `red-500`
- Confirmation required
- Not in easy reach zone

#### Category Colors (Quick Access)
- Jobs: Emerald (`emerald-500`)
- Property: Blue (`blue-500`)
- Talent: Purple (`purple-500`)
- Consistent across app

### 6. PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS

#### Critical Metrics
- First Contentful Paint: < 1.5s
- Time to Interactive: < 3.5s
- Cumulative Layout Shift: < 0.1

#### Optimization Rules
- Use `loading="lazy"` for images below fold
- Implement infinite scroll, not pagination
- Debounce search inputs (300ms)
- Use React.memo for list items
- Virtual scrolling for long lists (100+ items)

### 7. ACCESSIBILITY (A11Y)

#### REQUIRED
- All interactive elements have proper `aria-label`
- Keyboard navigation works
- Focus visible on all controls
- Color contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 (text)
- Color contrast ratio ≥ 3:1 (UI elements)

#### Touch/Click Areas
- Min 44x44px for WCAG AA
- Min 48x48px for WCAG AAA

### 8. FORM DESIGN

#### Mobile Forms
- One field per row
- Large inputs (h-12 to h-14)
- Show keyboard type hints
  - `type="email"` for email
  - `type="tel"` for phone
  - `inputMode="numeric"` for numbers
- Submit button at bottom (easy reach)
- Floating labels or placeholders

#### Desktop Forms
- 2-3 fields per row allowed
- Inline validation
- More compact spacing acceptable

### 9. SCROLLING & GESTURES

#### Horizontal Scrolling (Mobile)
```tsx
<div className="flex gap-3 overflow-x-auto snap-x snap-mandatory scrollbar-hide">
  <div className="snap-start shrink-0 w-[120px]">...</div>
</div>
```

#### Pull to Refresh
- Native feel
- Clear indicator
- Haptic feedback if possible

### 10. TYPOGRAPHY

#### Mobile
- Body: 14-16px
- Headings: 
  - H1: 24-28px
  - H2: 20-24px
  - H3: 18-20px
- Line height: 1.5 minimum
- Max 60 characters per line

#### Desktop  
- Body: 16px
- Headings: Can be larger
- Max 80 characters per line

### 11. SPACING SYSTEM (Tailwind)

#### Mobile Spacing
- Section padding: `py-6 px-4`
- Card padding: `p-4`
- Gap between items: `gap-3`

#### Desktop Spacing
- Section padding: `lg:py-10 lg:px-8`
- Card padding: `lg:p-6`
- Gap between items: `lg:gap-6`

### 12. IMAGES & MEDIA

#### Responsive Images
```tsx
<Image
  src={src}
  alt={alt}
  width={400}
  height={300}
  className="w-full h-auto"
  loading="lazy"
  placeholder="blur"
/>
```

#### Image Sizes
- Mobile thumbnail: 80-120px
- Desktop thumbnail: 200-300px
- Hero images: Responsive, max 1920px width

### 13. ERROR HANDLING

#### User-Friendly Errors
- NO technical jargon
- Clear action to resolve
- Inline validation, not alerts
- Toast notifications (bottom on mobile)

#### Example
❌ "Error 500: Internal Server Error"
✅ "Oops! Something went wrong. Please try again."

### 14. DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW

#### Before Coding
1. Check: Is this mobile-first?
2. Check: Are touch targets large enough?
3. Check: Is it in thumb reach zone?
4. Check: Different UI for mobile vs desktop?

#### Code Review Checklist
- [ ] Works on 320px width?
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ 44px?
- [ ] Horizontal scroll on mobile works?
- [ ] Bottom nav hidden on desktop?
- [ ] Active states on mobile?
- [ ] Hover states on desktop only?
- [ ] No content under bottom nav?
- [ ] Loading states implemented?

### 15. COMPONENTS LIBRARY STANDARDS

#### Button Component
```tsx
// Primary - Large touch target
<Button 
  size="lg"           // h-12 to h-14
  variant="primary"   // bg-emerald-500
  fullWidth          // w-full on mobile
  className="active:scale-95 lg:hover:bg-emerald-600"
>
  Action
</Button>
```

#### Card Component
```tsx
// Mobile-friendly card
<Card className="
  p-4 
  min-h-[120px]
  rounded-2xl 
  border-2
  active:scale-95
  lg:hover:shadow-xl
">
  Content
</Card>
```

### 16. STATE MANAGEMENT

#### Loading States
- Skeleton screens preferred
- Inline loading indicators
- NO full-page spinners on mobile

#### Error States  
- Retry button always visible
- Clear error message
- Maintain scroll position

### 17. SEARCH & FILTERING

#### Mobile
- Full-screen search overlay
- Large search input (h-12+)
- Filters in bottom sheet
- Swipe to close

#### Desktop
- Inline search bar
- Side panel filters
- Instant results

### 18. COPY & CONTENT

#### Mobile Copy
- Short and concise
- Action-oriented
- 1-2 sentences max
- Use bullet points

#### Button Text
- Action verbs: "Search", "Book", "Apply"
- Max 2 words on mobile
- Clear, not clever

### 19. TESTING REQUIREMENTS

#### Must Test On
- iPhone SE (375px) - smallest modern phone
- iPhone 14 Pro (390px)
- Android mid-range (360px)
- iPad (768px)
- Desktop (1920px)

#### Test Scenarios
- Thumb navigation only (no mouse)
- Slow 3G network
- Landscape orientation
- Dark mode

### 20. ANIMATION GUIDELINES

#### Mobile
- Quick animations (150-200ms)
- Use transform (GPU-accelerated)
- `transition-transform duration-150`

#### Desktop
- Slower animations acceptable (200-300ms)
- More elaborate hover effects
- Parallax OK

---

## 🚨 ABSOLUTE RULES (NEVER BREAK)

1. **ALWAYS design for mobile FIRST**
2. **NEVER** make touch targets smaller than 44x44px
3. **ALWAYS** hide bottom nav on desktop (`lg:hidden`)
4. **NEVER** put important actions in top corners on mobile
5. **ALWAYS** provide active feedback on mobile taps
6. **NEVER** use hover-only interactions on mobile
7. **ALWAYS** test on actual devices, not just DevTools
8. **NEVER** assume fast internet connection
9. **ALWAYS** provide offline fallbacks
10. **NEVER** use more than 3 columns on mobile

---

## 📝 QUICK REFERENCE: Common Patterns

### Horizontal Scroll Section (Mobile)
```tsx
<div className="lg:hidden">
  <div className="flex gap-3 overflow-x-auto snap-x snap-mandatory scrollbar-hide px-4">
    {items.map(item => (
      <div key={item.id} className="snap-start shrink-0 w-[120px] h-[120px]">
        {item.content}
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</div>
```

### Grid Section (Desktop)
```tsx
<div className="hidden lg:grid grid-cols-5 gap-4">
  {items.slice(0, 15).map(item => (
    <div key={item.id}>
      {item.content}
    </div>
  ))}
</div>
```

### Touch-Friendly Button
```tsx
<button className="
  h-14 px-6 
  rounded-2xl 
  bg-emerald-500 text-white
  font-semibold
  active:scale-95
  lg:hover:bg-emerald-600
  transition-all
  shadow-lg
">
  Action
</button>
```

---

## 🎨 Design System Quick Ref

### Colors
- Primary: `emerald-500` to `emerald-600`
- Secondary: `blue-500`, `purple-500`
- Text: `slate-900` (dark) / `white` (on dark bg)
- Background: `slate-100` (light mode), `slate-950` (dark mode)

### Spacing Scale (use these values)
- `gap-3` (12px) - Mobile items
- `gap-4` (16px) - Desktop items
- `p-4` (16px) - Mobile padding
- `p-6` (24px) - Desktop padding
- `py-6` (24px) - Mobile section padding
- `py-10` (40px) - Desktop section padding

### Border Radius
- `rounded-xl` (12px) - Buttons, inputs
- `rounded-2xl` (16px) - Cards, large elements

### Shadows
- `shadow-lg` - Mobile cards
- `shadow-xl` - Desktop hover
- `shadow-emerald-500/30` - Colored shadows

---

**Remember**: When in doubt, optimize for mobile thumb usage. Desktop is the enhancement, not the baseline.
